From 84030f99ffcce723481d21482547046d5842a22a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 06:46:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(code-skew): record the boot revision in hermes_bootstrap,
 before main imports the tree [daveey]

The boot-pin guard took its boot commit in start_gateway / the serve lifespan, after
hermes_cli.main had already imported much of the tree. A hermes update landing in that gap
passed as the boot commit, so the finder saw no skew and a lazy import (code_kernel) loaded
new code next to old eager modules (process_identity): ImportError 'spawn_owned'
(agent-529f2244ac, mini 2026-10-29; first occurrence t_01a1824adc287c5a).

- hermes_cli/git_fingerprint.py: stdlib-only fingerprint reader (moved from main.py, aliases kept)
  plus a per-process first-value-wins boot record.
- hermes_bootstrap records it right after the interrupted-update repair, before any other
  tree import; code_skew.record_boot_fingerprint prefers it and warns when HEAD already moved.
- Detection: code_skew.note_import_error logs one 'code-skew import mix' WARNING naming both
  shas when a tool dispatch or execute_code session kernel raises ImportError under skew.
- Tests: update-between-start-and-bootstrap regression, bootstrap wiring subprocess test,
  import-mix warning on the registry and session-kernel paths.
